From 639605235961bd39ffdb2664dd929ec819b168df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c4ffein <c4ffein.work@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 07:20:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add e2e tests for every deck (bun + playwright)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`bun test tests/e2e` serves the repo with Bun.serve, opens each slides/*.html
in headless Chromium and checks it against a golden structure file
(tests/e2e/golden/<deck>.json: every slide's h/v index, id, first heading,
start of its text, fragment count, plus the number of Reveal.next() steps to
reach the end). It also fails on console errors, page errors, failed
requests and 4xx/5xx responses while loading and while stepping through
every slide, checks each terminal recording mounted without an error line,
and opens the first transcript link to check the modal loads the viewer
without moving the deck.

Requests to other origins are blocked so the run is hermetic, and Reveal's
lazy data-src iframe cancellations (net::ERR_ABORTED) are ignored — a
missing file is a 404, which is caught.

UPDATE_GOLDEN=1 rewrites the goldens; SCREENSHOTS=1 dumps one PNG per slide
as a review aid; PW_CHROMIUM points at a local Chromium. A GitHub Actions
workflow runs the suite on push and pull request.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
